WEBVTT

00:42.250 --> 00:43.168
Ju-ran.

00:44.419 --> 00:46.337
Can you hear your Dad's voice now?

00:48.173 --> 00:50.383
It was the first thing I ever heard.

00:50.967 --> 00:52.677
The sound of warmth.

01:22.123 --> 01:23.583
But the fairy tale

01:24.709 --> 01:26.920
did not have a happy ending.

01:32.967 --> 01:34.511
Help! Over here!

01:34.594 --> 01:36.471
Father!

01:36.554 --> 01:39.265
Father!

02:08.962 --> 02:10.088
Run away.

02:10.171 --> 02:11.381
You have to run, Ju-ran.

02:11.464 --> 02:14.092
I will come and find you, so until then,

02:14.634 --> 02:17.303
keep yourself hidden
and don't get caught, okay?

02:21.099 --> 02:22.934
Go!

02:36.072 --> 02:36.990
Let's go.

02:39.450 --> 02:42.370
The children decided
to keep their identities secret

02:42.453 --> 02:44.873
and live in hiding,

02:45.456 --> 02:47.584
waiting for their father
to keep his promise

02:48.084 --> 02:50.336
and return to them.

02:53.339 --> 02:55.341
If you're deaf,
you should at least be sharp.

02:55.425 --> 02:58.094
If you're not sharp,
you could at least be handy.

02:58.178 --> 03:00.054
What a pain!

03:03.975 --> 03:04.893
Ju-ran.

03:17.614 --> 03:18.573
It's me, Dad.

03:20.700 --> 03:24.037
But the fairy tale did not end there.

04:01.991 --> 04:03.534
Will that be enough?

04:03.618 --> 04:05.745
We have to start somewhere.

04:07.664 --> 04:09.791
You kids focus on
finding the Child of Eternity.

04:11.793 --> 04:14.003
That's the only thing
that will get us closer

04:14.545 --> 04:16.214
to a cure for the side effects.

04:17.548 --> 04:19.425
The children realized

04:20.468 --> 04:23.304
that only by finding
the child with the heart of eternity

04:23.972 --> 04:25.723
could all of this

04:26.307 --> 04:29.143
reach a happy ending.

04:33.731 --> 04:36.276
I heard you were released on parole.

04:37.026 --> 04:38.653
A year ago, I believe.

04:39.320 --> 04:42.740
I was in there for over 20 years.

04:43.866 --> 04:46.703
I'm sure it was
hardly enough time to recall

04:47.245 --> 04:48.997
the faces of all the dead children.

04:49.080 --> 04:52.041
You never even cared about them
in the first place.

04:53.543 --> 04:55.837
Whatever happened to those children,

04:55.920 --> 04:59.424
abandoned, abused,
and wandering listlessly…

05:00.216 --> 05:01.092
You never cared.

05:02.760 --> 05:05.388
My children and I risked everything

05:05.471 --> 05:08.683
for that immortality project of yours.

05:09.183 --> 05:12.353
And though, yes,
some sacrifices were made,

05:13.104 --> 05:14.272
I was successful.

05:16.065 --> 05:19.485
And yet, to be treated as I was,
like a criminal…

05:21.154 --> 05:22.447
I must say, I was hurt.

05:23.281 --> 05:24.490
It seems that one of us

05:25.116 --> 05:27.577
has been laboring
under a grave misunderstanding.

05:29.245 --> 05:31.622
I didn't fund and support you

05:32.165 --> 05:34.292
because I wanted you to succeed.

05:34.834 --> 05:36.544
It was for the suffering children.

05:37.962 --> 05:40.882
I wonder if believing that
eases your conscience.

05:45.511 --> 05:47.597
I heard that you, Madam King,

05:48.097 --> 05:50.433
took in most of the rescued children.

05:50.516 --> 05:53.019
I found every one of them new families

05:53.644 --> 05:55.521
or sent them to study abroad.

05:55.605 --> 05:56.439
Why do you ask?

05:57.774 --> 05:58.983
And the Child of Eternity?

06:04.655 --> 06:06.532
So you've seen the Child of Eternity.

06:09.077 --> 06:10.161
Where is that child?

06:50.076 --> 06:51.786
Let me ask you again.

06:52.286 --> 06:55.039
Where is the Child of Eternity now?

06:57.583 --> 07:01.462
Director Choi already told me everything
with his last breath.

07:02.422 --> 07:05.716
That only you, Madam King of Hearty House,

07:06.551 --> 07:08.386
know where the Child of Eternity is.

07:09.720 --> 07:11.055
Answer him.

07:18.980 --> 07:19.814
That child…

07:26.237 --> 07:27.321
is dead.

07:32.243 --> 07:33.161
What did you say?

07:34.996 --> 07:36.539
Dead.

07:39.625 --> 07:42.211
The Child of Eternity cannot die.

07:53.431 --> 07:56.184
-One more time.
-No, please. Stop.

07:56.267 --> 07:58.478
-It's okay.
-I'm scared.

07:58.561 --> 08:01.189
-Please stop.
-Stop it.

08:01.272 --> 08:02.940
No, please stop. I'm scared.

08:03.024 --> 08:04.484
Can't you hear me?

08:04.567 --> 08:07.028
-I'm scared. Please, no.
-Hurry.

08:07.111 --> 08:09.822
Please stop. No.

08:09.906 --> 08:11.449
Stop it.

08:12.700 --> 08:14.243
But immortality doesn't mean

08:15.453 --> 08:17.079
immunity to pain.

08:19.081 --> 08:20.291
Every moment,

08:20.875 --> 08:23.461
with each and every death.

08:33.846 --> 08:35.014
One more time!

08:35.097 --> 08:36.974
-No, I'm scared!
-It's okay.

08:37.058 --> 08:38.601
Please stop!

08:38.684 --> 08:40.019
I said stop!

08:41.062 --> 08:42.438
-Stop it!
-Don't do this.

08:46.776 --> 08:48.694
-Please don't do this.
-One more time!

08:48.778 --> 08:50.613
Stop!

08:52.990 --> 08:54.867
I told you to stop.

08:54.951 --> 08:55.993
Stop!

08:57.328 --> 08:58.579
Stop it!

08:59.205 --> 09:00.915
Just stop it!

09:34.031 --> 09:37.034
Ma'am, how much rice should we use?

09:40.580 --> 09:41.664
Rice.

09:41.747 --> 09:44.458
How much should we soak
for the celebratory rice cakes?

09:44.542 --> 09:45.710
Right.

09:46.502 --> 09:48.796
You should soak about three to five mal.

09:48.879 --> 09:50.965
So how much exactly?

09:51.048 --> 09:53.092
Three mal or four mal?

09:53.175 --> 09:54.135
Or five mal?

09:54.635 --> 09:58.723
Goodness, what's gotten into you?
You're usually so precise.

09:59.724 --> 10:01.058
Hey, Won-ju.

10:02.059 --> 10:02.893
Yes?

10:02.977 --> 10:05.271
Didn't someone come by just now?

10:05.354 --> 10:07.273
Who would've come by?

10:07.356 --> 10:09.275
You've been sitting alone the whole time.

10:09.859 --> 10:11.277
And how much red bean?

10:11.777 --> 10:13.487
Three to five mal of that too?

10:13.571 --> 10:15.364
What on earth happened here?

10:15.448 --> 10:16.282
Goodness me.

10:16.365 --> 10:18.743
Was there an earthquake or something?

10:18.826 --> 10:21.787
Goodness, how completely bizarre.

10:21.871 --> 10:25.249
They say the apocalypse is coming.
Maybe the world really is about to end.

10:25.333 --> 10:26.959
Or maybe someone upset the spirits?

10:27.043 --> 10:30.087
Why are all these
strange things happening?

11:11.545 --> 11:12.630
Pretty.

11:13.839 --> 11:15.841
Should I go to see the Northern Lights?

11:15.925 --> 11:17.593
I heard they're breathtaking.

11:18.427 --> 11:19.345
Hold up.

11:20.429 --> 11:22.848
Couldn't I just teleport there?

11:23.766 --> 11:24.684
No way.

11:25.351 --> 11:27.353
Does that mean I can save on airfares?

11:28.604 --> 11:30.564
Hey, that's pretty awesome!

11:31.607 --> 11:32.817
Pretty darn awesome!

11:43.786 --> 11:45.162
ABILITY: GRAVITY
RANK: S

11:47.540 --> 11:49.375
ABILITY: HALLUCINATION
GRADE: S

11:51.836 --> 11:54.046
ABILITY: BRAINWASHING
RANK: S

12:48.392 --> 12:52.104
THE WONDERFOOLS

12:53.314 --> 12:57.985
EPISODE 4
BOON THE KING DUCK VS WUNDERKINDER

13:22.384 --> 13:23.886
Hey, I used to use that thing.

13:23.969 --> 13:27.097
I heard retro is in these days.
Are you into it too?

13:27.181 --> 13:30.184
My CD player broke,
and apparently, it's beyond repair.

13:31.268 --> 13:34.480
Mom says I should save for a new one,
but it'll take forever.

13:34.563 --> 13:35.481
Hey, wait.

13:38.067 --> 13:40.194
How about I get you one for your birthday?

13:40.778 --> 13:42.071
For which birthday?

13:42.655 --> 13:45.407
With your allowance,
I'd have to wait until I'm 40 to get it.

13:47.409 --> 13:48.494
Hey, your lunchbox.

13:57.920 --> 13:59.255
Have a good day, sweetie.

14:07.429 --> 14:09.473
How's this thing broken exactly?

14:17.523 --> 14:19.400
Thousand, ten thousand, hundred thousand…

14:21.777 --> 14:24.488
At this price, I couldn't afford it
by her 60th birthday,

14:24.989 --> 14:26.448
let alone her 40th.

14:33.122 --> 14:35.833
Cheong, you overestimate your old man.

14:42.006 --> 14:42.840
Hello?

14:44.049 --> 14:46.051
What do you want, Lady Trainwreck?

14:46.802 --> 14:49.638
Let's go home, shall we?
Mr. Coo-coo, let's go home.

14:49.722 --> 14:52.725
Let's go home. Back to your happy home.

14:52.808 --> 14:55.144
Come on, now. Let's go.

14:56.020 --> 14:57.646
Let's go.

15:09.325 --> 15:10.242
Master!

15:32.932 --> 15:34.058
Why are you all…

15:34.141 --> 15:37.019
You asked if we were free on Friday.
And they both were.

15:37.102 --> 15:38.062
All right.

15:38.729 --> 15:41.649
How does it feel to have the calvary
on your team, Master?

15:41.732 --> 15:45.027
Calvary is where Jesus was crucified.
You mean the cavalry.

15:45.110 --> 15:46.612
Get off me.

15:47.863 --> 15:52.117
I must say, you're smarter
than I thought, Mr. Oddball.

15:52.201 --> 15:56.497
Who knew you'd give us special training
disguised as Civil Complaints Office work?

15:57.081 --> 15:58.749
We'll be paid for this, right?

15:59.583 --> 16:00.459
Special training?

16:01.835 --> 16:03.295
You were totally rad.

16:03.796 --> 16:06.674
Lifting things, not to mention my heart,
up and down with one finger!

16:06.757 --> 16:08.092
It was totally--

16:08.175 --> 16:09.051
What are you doing?

16:09.843 --> 16:12.471
As for me,
my heart was brimming with excitement.

16:12.554 --> 16:16.266
Like I've become a real civil servant.
And now, you're offering to teach us.

16:16.350 --> 16:19.269
Does this mean
we can become as cool as you, Master?

16:19.353 --> 16:21.480
Thank you so much!

16:21.563 --> 16:23.273
I will never forget this kindness!

16:23.357 --> 16:24.400
You kiss-ass.

16:24.483 --> 16:27.528
Mr. Lee Un-jeong. Very good!
You've finally put together a team?

16:27.611 --> 16:29.363
-Two, three!
-Hello!

16:29.446 --> 16:32.533
We're Team Lee Un-jeong
from the Haeseong Civil Complaints Office!

16:32.616 --> 16:34.118
At your service!

16:37.121 --> 16:37.955
Are you for real?

16:39.832 --> 16:40.874
Yes, well…

16:40.958 --> 16:44.211
Now, Mr. Lee Un-jeong here
has many shortcomings,

16:44.294 --> 16:46.422
so I'm sure you must be worried, Mr. Yang.

16:46.505 --> 16:47.548
But

16:48.090 --> 16:49.341
he's got us now, see?

16:51.218 --> 16:55.639
We'll make up for all of his shortcomings,
so don't you worry.

16:55.723 --> 16:56.557
Sure.

16:57.349 --> 17:00.602
Well, then, before my worries
get the better of me…

17:00.686 --> 17:01.937
Bring it in.

17:02.438 --> 17:03.772
Let's do this. Good.

17:06.150 --> 17:07.317
I'll see you later!

17:07.401 --> 17:08.777
Don't you worry!

17:10.487 --> 17:12.698
What's that? The bus? Over here, everyone.

17:12.781 --> 17:14.324
Careful. Watch out for the bus.

17:14.408 --> 17:17.077
Okay, keep it coming.

17:17.161 --> 17:19.204
Keep coming. That's it.

17:21.373 --> 17:23.500
Stop!

17:23.584 --> 17:24.418
All right.

17:24.918 --> 17:26.378
CHURCH OF ETERNAL SALVATION

17:27.796 --> 17:29.798
Why is the Church
of Eternal Salvation here?

17:30.382 --> 17:33.093
-Why are those cultists here?
-Must be here to recruit us.

17:34.428 --> 17:37.097
Special orders from the mayor,
so no grumbling, okay?

17:37.181 --> 17:40.893
Any unnecessary complaining,
and all contract staff could be let go.

17:41.769 --> 17:44.229
Why, yes. There you are. Hello.

17:44.313 --> 17:45.189
All right.

17:45.272 --> 17:47.816
Today is our street clean-up drive,

17:47.900 --> 17:51.653
and members of the Church
of Eternal Salvation will be helping us.

17:51.737 --> 17:53.906
Let's welcome them
with a round of applause!

17:53.989 --> 17:55.491
Let's give them a hand!

17:55.574 --> 17:58.494
-Welcome, all! Yes!
-My goodness.

17:59.453 --> 18:02.039
Thank you for the warm welcome.

18:03.082 --> 18:07.044
When it comes to cleaning up Haeseong,
of course we should help out.

18:09.046 --> 18:11.173
Trash should be collected immediately

18:11.256 --> 18:14.051
to make the world
a clean and beautiful place.

18:14.134 --> 18:16.637
Yes, you're absolutely right.

18:16.720 --> 18:17.554
Collecting?

18:18.055 --> 18:20.599
To cleanse the world
and make it beautiful.

18:23.268 --> 18:25.104
Can we talk for a moment?

18:27.106 --> 18:27.940
Come on.

18:28.941 --> 18:31.235
Man, he's got us running
all over the place.

18:35.280 --> 18:36.406
Why are we here?

18:41.120 --> 18:43.789
The work's just a front
for us to train here, isn't it?

18:43.872 --> 18:45.499
Of course.

18:45.582 --> 18:48.001
We can't do our special training
out in the open.

18:48.085 --> 18:49.253
We have to be discreet.

18:50.838 --> 18:51.964
No special training.

18:52.047 --> 18:53.841
-Are you kidding?
-What?

18:55.801 --> 18:58.887
People only envy and admire people
with abilities like ours

18:59.388 --> 19:00.389
in movies.

19:01.223 --> 19:03.725
People fear and avoid
those who are different.

19:04.226 --> 19:06.353
They are shunned and despised.

19:06.436 --> 19:09.481
People already fear and avoid
Lady Trainwreck here.

19:10.315 --> 19:12.651
Should I show you why
right here, right now?

19:19.408 --> 19:20.450
This is it.

19:22.619 --> 19:25.581
To live normal lives,
you must control and hide your abilities.

19:26.248 --> 19:27.666
If someone finds out

19:28.500 --> 19:31.128
and if that someone
is very intrigued by your abilities,

19:33.338 --> 19:34.464
you might never

19:35.090 --> 19:35.966
get to see…

19:37.968 --> 19:41.597
your friends, family,
or those you cherish ever again.

19:47.436 --> 19:50.772
So we'd really get carted off
if we're caught?

19:51.565 --> 19:53.275
Never get to see them again?

19:54.026 --> 19:56.028
No special training would suffice.

19:56.528 --> 19:58.614
Everyone's abilities manifest differently,

19:58.697 --> 20:00.949
so you have to figure out
your own abilities.

20:01.033 --> 20:05.245
And how exactly do we figure that out?
That's what we've been asking you.

20:05.329 --> 20:06.330
Repetition.

20:07.497 --> 20:11.627
The only option is repeated practice.
There will be some kind of rule.

20:12.127 --> 20:15.130
Focus on when and in what situations
your abilities manifest.

20:16.757 --> 20:20.594
No one leaves this place today
until they've figured something out.

20:22.221 --> 20:24.890
Like a fiery test by fire.

20:24.973 --> 20:26.141
Trial by fire.

20:26.725 --> 20:28.894
Isn't that a bit too hardcore,
Mr. Oddball?

20:28.977 --> 20:30.646
Can't you go easy on us?

20:31.146 --> 20:33.774
You're not going to lock us up in here

20:33.857 --> 20:35.984
and ship us off in this container,
are you?

20:36.068 --> 20:38.570
Come on, who would buy
a shipping container full of us?

20:38.654 --> 20:41.114
He's just pushing us so we learn faster.

20:41.198 --> 20:43.533
Understood.
I'll do my best to learn, Master.

20:43.617 --> 20:44.826
Is that what you're doing?

20:47.496 --> 20:49.122
Lock the door from the outside.

20:49.206 --> 20:51.959
-Okay! Let's give it a try.
-Wait, the door?

20:52.042 --> 20:52.960
Let's do this!

20:53.043 --> 20:55.796
Is locking the door really necessary?

21:00.008 --> 21:01.176
This isn't too shabby.

21:05.555 --> 21:06.890
Let's take one of each.

21:06.974 --> 21:08.684
You punk, can't you see I'm hurt?

21:14.064 --> 21:16.525
So we saved them?

21:20.237 --> 21:23.740
We're pretty awesome,

21:23.824 --> 21:25.367
aren't we?

21:30.747 --> 21:31.623
No.

21:32.124 --> 21:33.750
That's not me.

21:34.710 --> 21:35.794
I'm just…

21:40.924 --> 21:41.925
Dr. Ha.

21:52.936 --> 21:55.355
His vitals are also declining.

22:00.986 --> 22:02.195
Scrap him.

22:13.832 --> 22:16.001
We won't end up like that
one day, will we?

22:19.755 --> 22:21.465
If we can't fix the side effects,

22:22.299 --> 22:23.967
we could get deformed like that too.

22:25.510 --> 22:28.722
I just wonder if we'll end up
gasping for air, unable to breathe,

22:28.805 --> 22:31.350
and ultimately scrapped, just like them.

22:32.476 --> 22:33.310
Don't you

22:35.062 --> 22:36.313
trust Father?

22:38.523 --> 22:40.776
I do know he's hiding something from us.

22:41.276 --> 22:42.319
Like about 3972.

22:43.612 --> 22:46.281
Father does everything
for a reason, Ho-ran.

22:46.365 --> 22:49.159
Yeah, I'm sure he does.

22:50.494 --> 22:52.204
But I'm not sure if that reason

22:52.704 --> 22:55.082
is for our good.

22:55.165 --> 22:58.126
Stop thinking useless thoughts
and go do your job.

22:58.835 --> 23:01.755
Because if we fail to find
the Child of Eternity…

23:04.383 --> 23:07.511
all that awaits us,
Father included, is death.

23:08.512 --> 23:11.056
Okay, I got it.

24:05.861 --> 24:06.862
My goodness!

24:10.115 --> 24:12.033
-My congratulations!
-Oh my.

24:12.117 --> 24:13.827
Have a read before you go in!

24:13.910 --> 24:15.662
-Oh my!
-Congratulations!

24:15.745 --> 24:17.581
-Go in now.
-She got a job?

24:17.664 --> 24:20.459
-Congratulations!
-Thank you.

24:22.169 --> 24:24.212
So do you think it can be restored?

24:24.296 --> 24:26.381
No, it doesn't seem likely.

24:27.716 --> 24:31.011
It wasn't just overwritten
but completely erased by a magnetic field.

24:32.387 --> 24:35.557
I spent a fortune installing
those security cameras or whatnot,

24:35.640 --> 24:36.933
but they're darn useless.

24:37.017 --> 24:39.603
One camera managed to capture something.

24:39.686 --> 24:40.687
What?

24:43.565 --> 24:44.608
The camera out back.

25:06.338 --> 25:07.255
What is it?

25:08.924 --> 25:12.594
It's that woman.
The variant 3972 hangs out with.

25:18.600 --> 25:19.434
What should we do?

25:22.103 --> 25:22.979
Collect her.

25:37.160 --> 25:39.538
If this works, it'll be huge.

25:39.621 --> 25:43.750
The northern lights.
It'd be great if I could really go there.

25:45.502 --> 25:46.545
The northern lights.

25:47.045 --> 25:48.922
How awesome would that be?

25:50.840 --> 25:52.217
Let's go. Yeah.

25:52.968 --> 25:53.843
Let's go!

25:57.013 --> 25:58.265
Guess not.

25:58.348 --> 25:59.933
Okay, focus.

26:02.852 --> 26:03.853
And I'm still here.

26:04.354 --> 26:05.605
Okay, focus now.

26:17.951 --> 26:18.785
Did you see that?

26:18.868 --> 26:20.620
What on earth happened

26:21.454 --> 26:22.872
to my Chae-ni just now?

26:24.082 --> 26:25.333
Did she just vanish?

26:26.876 --> 26:29.045
Did you succeed? Where did you go? Norway?

26:29.129 --> 26:30.088
Finland?

26:30.171 --> 26:31.715
Did you really see the aurora?

26:36.219 --> 26:37.053
I did.

26:37.137 --> 26:38.638
AURORA

26:39.139 --> 26:42.809
Put a name tag on my chest…

26:42.892 --> 26:43.935
I'm here, baby.

26:44.019 --> 26:45.145
Cheers!

26:47.939 --> 26:49.524
Deary me. Miss?

26:50.692 --> 26:52.819
No, don't go. Why are you leaving?

26:53.320 --> 26:54.654
Come again tomorrow.

26:55.155 --> 26:56.281
She's cute.

27:00.493 --> 27:01.328
How pathetic.

27:01.411 --> 27:03.913
I'd expect nothing less from a half-wit.

27:03.997 --> 27:06.750
Cut her some slack. She half-succeeded.

27:06.833 --> 27:07.792
Well done, Chae-ni.

27:07.876 --> 27:10.170
Do you find this funny, Mr. Son?

27:10.670 --> 27:12.881
Would it be funny
if Cheong saw you get stuck?

27:12.964 --> 27:15.717
Hey, keep family out of this.

27:15.800 --> 27:18.637
Then stop slacking off and practice.

27:18.720 --> 27:22.057
I'm super scared that I'll end up
disappearing in front of Grandma.

27:22.140 --> 27:24.267
She'd probably keel over from shock.

27:24.768 --> 27:25.852
That's not all.

27:25.935 --> 27:28.730
I'd be locked up forever
in the biggest hospital in Seoul.

27:29.230 --> 27:32.984
I'm more scared of Grandma finding out
than being carted off somewhere.

27:33.068 --> 27:35.028
I'm super desperate too.

27:35.528 --> 27:37.113
Do you know what my dream is?

27:37.656 --> 27:38.865
It's to be Uri Geller.

27:39.783 --> 27:40.950
Your dream

27:41.660 --> 27:42.994
is to be a con artist?

27:43.078 --> 27:44.829
You're so clueless.

27:45.330 --> 27:48.792
Uri Geller is a real psychic,
and he makes a ton of money.

27:51.127 --> 27:52.003
This.

27:52.796 --> 27:54.339
If I could gift one of these

27:54.422 --> 27:56.591
to each of Cheong's classmates,
I'd die happy.

27:58.760 --> 27:59.594
If I'm honest,

28:00.095 --> 28:03.098
like Mr. Son,
I also have something I'd like to do.

28:03.181 --> 28:04.015
What?

28:04.516 --> 28:05.975
Well, thanks to you,

28:06.059 --> 28:08.937
I had a pretty easy time in high school,

28:09.562 --> 28:11.856
but middle school was pretty rough.

28:11.940 --> 28:15.026
I want to go and revisit every kid
who bullied me back then.

28:16.069 --> 28:18.738
Hey, Kang Ro-bin!

28:19.823 --> 28:21.866
Is the worm finally tuning?

28:21.950 --> 28:24.994
What would you do to them?
Hurt them? Get revenge?

28:25.078 --> 28:26.830
No.

28:28.039 --> 28:28.998
I want to brag.

28:30.208 --> 28:31.793
That I've become really strong.

28:32.460 --> 28:34.254
Typical Sappy Sap.

28:34.838 --> 28:37.507
Can't you just go on
a brutal, bloodstained revenge spree?

28:37.590 --> 28:39.634
A guy like me get revenge? No way.

28:40.135 --> 28:42.095
Besides, in some ways,

28:42.178 --> 28:44.764
I sort of feel bad for my superpower.

28:45.265 --> 28:47.809
If it had gone to someone cooler,

28:47.892 --> 28:51.271
they would've used it in cool ways,
saved people, and all that.

28:51.771 --> 28:54.941
But it had to come
to someone useless like me.

28:55.024 --> 28:56.568
Now it's really useless.

28:58.153 --> 29:02.240
I recently saw the historical drama
500 Years of the Joseon Dynasty.

29:02.991 --> 29:04.367
They had these scapeghosts.

29:04.451 --> 29:05.785
Scapegoat, you mean.

29:05.869 --> 29:08.329
Anyway, they were basically goalies.

29:08.830 --> 29:12.292
They'd use their bodies
to block and absorb all the bad energy

29:12.792 --> 29:14.085
to protect the royal court.

29:14.169 --> 29:15.754
What's that got to do with me?

29:17.213 --> 29:20.300
Who else could handle the Royal Nightmare,

29:20.383 --> 29:21.634
Lady Trainwreck,

29:21.718 --> 29:24.304
and the curmudgeonly old lady
of Hearty House?

29:24.804 --> 29:26.598
Who would keep the peace in Haeseong?

29:29.601 --> 29:32.854
First, let's just try to figure out
how to use these abilities.

29:32.937 --> 29:36.399
He said we could avoid being carted off
and live normal, quiet lives.

29:36.483 --> 29:38.568
And once we get used to them,

29:39.611 --> 29:43.490
I'll get you some undies to wear
over your tights, like Superman.

29:43.990 --> 29:46.576
Really? And I get to pick out the design?

29:46.659 --> 29:47.744
I dare you.

29:51.956 --> 29:52.874
Hello?

29:53.792 --> 29:54.626
Hey, Grandma.

29:55.126 --> 29:57.670
I'm busy with my public duties.
What is it now?

29:59.631 --> 30:00.548
Hello?

30:02.300 --> 30:03.384
Hello? Grandma?

30:03.468 --> 30:05.553
Just tell me where you are.

30:05.637 --> 30:08.014
Do your public duties later
and come home now.

30:08.556 --> 30:09.432
Never mind.

30:09.516 --> 30:11.434
I'll pick you up. Where are you now?

30:11.518 --> 30:12.352
Hello?

30:12.852 --> 30:14.229
-Grandma.
-Hello?

30:14.312 --> 30:15.730
-I can hear--
-Eunie?

30:15.814 --> 30:17.524
-Yes, Grandma--
-Eunie!

30:18.024 --> 30:18.858
Hello?

30:19.442 --> 30:21.236
-Hello? Grandma!
-Where are you?

30:23.279 --> 30:24.656
Hey, Gunie.

30:24.739 --> 30:27.784
Hurry back to the office
and find out where Eun Chae-ni is.

30:27.867 --> 30:28.701
Sorry?

30:29.536 --> 30:30.954
Right, okay.

30:34.290 --> 30:35.166
But, Ms. Kim,

30:36.209 --> 30:37.669
I guess you weren't aware

30:37.752 --> 30:40.421
that Eun Chae-ni had such an ability.

30:46.261 --> 30:47.262
Hello?

30:48.638 --> 30:50.139
Hey, Jun-mo.

30:53.893 --> 30:55.395
About Chae-ni.

30:55.478 --> 30:58.606
Looks like she's working hard
at the Civil Complaints Office.

31:00.567 --> 31:02.902
She hasn't budged an inch from City Hall.

31:03.862 --> 31:04.988
I see.

31:06.698 --> 31:07.991
And you're doing good?

31:08.074 --> 31:09.534
Of course.

31:10.034 --> 31:12.745
You'll be the first to know
if anything happens, Grandma.

31:15.039 --> 31:15.999
That's it.

31:16.666 --> 31:19.752
Jun-mo has always called me Grandma.

31:20.336 --> 31:23.172
He's never called me "Ms. Kim."

31:26.634 --> 31:28.636
Damn, you caught me.

31:29.804 --> 31:32.515
It's always the little details
that give me away.

31:56.080 --> 31:57.415
Whose daughter are you?

31:57.498 --> 31:59.167
Dr. Ha Won-do.

31:59.250 --> 32:00.460
He's my father.

32:01.377 --> 32:02.211
You

32:03.588 --> 32:05.506
call that man your father?

32:05.590 --> 32:07.800
He's the only one who took us in.

32:08.593 --> 32:09.844
I guess I'm to blame.

32:11.095 --> 32:12.847
I failed to take care of you all.

32:16.267 --> 32:18.811
Don't say things you don't mean.

32:18.895 --> 32:21.439
We know you only saved the kids
without abilities.

32:26.110 --> 32:28.780
You were afraid of the world
finding out we existed,

32:29.280 --> 32:30.239
weren't you?

32:31.950 --> 32:34.285
That's why you didn't save
the Wunderkinder.

32:34.369 --> 32:37.830
You just left us to die
in that burning lab.

32:39.457 --> 32:41.042
Did Ha Won-do tell you that?

32:41.876 --> 32:43.127
Child, that's not true.

32:43.211 --> 32:45.171
You only took the Child of Eternity.

32:47.632 --> 32:52.220
You guys only took the Child of Eternity,
who you needed, and as for the rest of us…

32:55.098 --> 32:56.099
you abandoned us.

32:57.684 --> 32:58.893
So that's it.

32:59.894 --> 33:00.979
The reason you're here.

33:04.607 --> 33:05.566
Where are they now?

33:05.650 --> 33:06.818
The child's dead.

33:08.403 --> 33:12.240
My sister's ability may not have worked
on you, but don't underestimate mine.

33:12.782 --> 33:16.202
I can make you experience

33:17.036 --> 33:17.996
hell on earth.

33:28.464 --> 33:29.424
Let me ask.

33:30.842 --> 33:33.553
Do I look like I'm in a good place to you?

33:36.389 --> 33:39.559
After losing all those precious children,

33:40.226 --> 33:44.188
my own child was the one
who had to pay for that sin, not me.

33:48.985 --> 33:50.862
You needn't bother.

33:51.863 --> 33:53.448
The past 20 years

33:53.948 --> 33:55.908
have already been hell on earth.

33:58.202 --> 34:00.163
Hello, we're here.

34:00.246 --> 34:01.914
-Hello.
-Please sit.

34:01.998 --> 34:04.250
-Welcome.
-Yes, hello.

34:04.333 --> 34:06.461
-Welcome.
-Whatever you want to eat.

34:07.003 --> 34:09.172
-Welcome.
-What should we eat?

34:13.718 --> 34:16.012
If that child really is dead,

34:17.430 --> 34:18.806
you'd better find the body.

34:20.850 --> 34:24.729
Or I'll show you true hell on earth.

34:31.986 --> 34:32.945
Did you hear that?

34:34.197 --> 34:35.156
You'd better go

34:36.199 --> 34:38.785
and find Chae-ni right now, Jun-mo.

34:42.622 --> 34:49.253
It is his will

34:49.337 --> 34:55.009
Forgive us our sins

34:55.551 --> 35:01.974
I will give my life

35:02.058 --> 35:07.313
To be saved

35:08.272 --> 35:14.195
A place where

35:14.278 --> 35:19.826
An endless paradise unfolds

35:20.326 --> 35:26.207
I will go to him

35:28.626 --> 35:30.336
Hey, look!

35:30.878 --> 35:34.132
Are we even sure there are rules?
I have no clue.

35:34.715 --> 35:36.926
Just sticking and unsticking willy-nilly.

35:37.009 --> 35:38.261
And the body part too.

35:38.970 --> 35:42.181
Sometimes it's my butt. Sometimes my arm.
It's completely random.

35:42.974 --> 35:45.643
There must be some kind of rule.
Think harder.

35:49.063 --> 35:50.523
You should think really hard.

35:50.606 --> 35:53.651
Don't you have the most to gain?
You'd have the strength of a tiger.

35:56.154 --> 35:56.988
Tears?

35:58.656 --> 35:59.907
I think I was crying.

36:06.247 --> 36:07.165
Tears.

36:07.248 --> 36:08.749
-He's crying.
-Try it now!

36:08.833 --> 36:10.001
Okay, straight punch.

36:10.084 --> 36:11.169
Okay, hi-yah!

36:11.252 --> 36:12.170
Okay.

36:13.588 --> 36:14.422
It didn't work?

36:15.840 --> 36:16.716
Hey, more tears.

36:16.799 --> 36:17.717
Let's try again.

36:17.800 --> 36:19.427
Put your back into it!

36:19.510 --> 36:20.344
Okay.

36:20.845 --> 36:21.762
Karate chop.

36:21.846 --> 36:23.764
-Hi-yah!
-Hi-yah!

36:25.975 --> 36:27.476
Go again. Hi-yah!

36:29.061 --> 36:30.354
I can't do it.

36:30.438 --> 36:32.857
Just hit it. What's a few broken fingers?

36:32.940 --> 36:33.816
It hurts.

36:33.900 --> 36:35.651
Don't just stand like this. Do it!

36:35.735 --> 36:37.862
Okay, just once. Okay, go!

36:37.945 --> 36:39.030
One, two.

36:39.572 --> 36:40.698
It hurts too much.

36:42.200 --> 36:43.868
Your tears are drying up.

36:43.951 --> 36:44.827
Go again?

36:44.911 --> 36:45.745
Hold on.

36:46.287 --> 36:47.413
It hurts.

36:48.873 --> 36:51.209
Hold your horses.

36:51.292 --> 36:54.462
I think I'm onto something.

36:54.962 --> 36:55.796
Run!

37:04.138 --> 37:05.932
Do I need to be out of breath?

37:07.767 --> 37:09.268
One, two!

37:09.977 --> 37:12.271
Hey, you punk! Why'd you hit me…

37:15.441 --> 37:17.693
Okay. Karate chop!

37:27.995 --> 37:29.413
I'll see you later.

37:33.334 --> 37:35.544
This is the end of my patrol area.

37:35.628 --> 37:37.296
This field is the last stop.

37:37.380 --> 37:38.214
I see.

37:40.091 --> 37:42.426
So this will be the last stop.

37:44.720 --> 37:46.222
Thank you for your help.

37:46.305 --> 37:48.516
I think I can take it from here.

37:48.599 --> 37:49.517
That's all right.

37:49.600 --> 37:52.979
I was told that we should see
the clean-up through to the end.

37:54.021 --> 37:54.939
Who said that?

37:55.022 --> 37:58.651
Who else?
Our very own shepherd, Kim Pal-ho.

38:01.862 --> 38:04.407
And it seems you have blind faith
in your shepherd.

38:05.783 --> 38:06.617
No.

38:07.326 --> 38:09.287
To believe or not to believe

38:09.370 --> 38:12.081
involves human will, does it not?

38:12.164 --> 38:15.126
We do not believe. We know.

38:17.461 --> 38:19.922
We are aware of the fact

38:20.423 --> 38:22.258
that the apocalypse is near.

38:23.801 --> 38:25.803
"The apocalypse will come."

38:25.886 --> 38:28.347
"There is no escaping that fact."

38:29.015 --> 38:33.269
"Everyone dies.
There is no escaping that fact."

38:33.853 --> 38:34.895
How are they different?

38:35.855 --> 38:37.064
The difference

38:37.148 --> 38:42.028
is that our shepherd knows when, where,
and how the apocalypse will happen.

38:42.111 --> 38:44.488
What's the point of
knowing about the apocalypse

38:44.989 --> 38:46.490
if you can't avoid it?

38:47.742 --> 38:49.952
That's right. It cannot be avoided.

38:50.036 --> 38:51.912
Not by foolish humans.

38:51.996 --> 38:55.541
But the Church of Eternal Salvation
is different.

38:55.624 --> 38:56.959
We can be saved.

39:00.671 --> 39:04.050
We have witnessed miracles
with our own two eyes.

39:04.133 --> 39:05.968
And we know that such miracles

39:06.510 --> 39:09.930
will be granted to us
at the moment of the apocalypse.

39:12.058 --> 39:14.810
Whatever you saw wasn't a miracle, but…

39:33.954 --> 39:35.831
Lord, are you with us?

39:37.166 --> 39:39.335
My Lord!

39:40.961 --> 39:43.589
My Lord! Please forgive us our sins.

39:43.672 --> 39:44.840
Please save us.

39:44.924 --> 39:48.969
Save all our believers
in the midst of the apocalypse!

39:49.470 --> 39:50.429
Are you here?

39:50.513 --> 39:52.056
Please forgive my sins.

39:52.139 --> 39:56.560
I am ready to give my life for you!

39:59.146 --> 40:01.774
Shepherd Kim Pal-ho asked me
to pass on a message.

40:01.857 --> 40:04.819
Number 3972,
your apocalypse shall take place

40:04.902 --> 40:06.362
right here, today,

40:06.445 --> 40:08.364
and there shall be no mercy.

41:40.789 --> 41:44.293
You laughed earlier, didn't you?
When he said "Shepherd Kim Pal-ho."

41:46.921 --> 41:48.297
What are you talking about?

41:48.797 --> 41:49.715
You crazy bastard!

42:01.727 --> 42:05.231
Didn't you know that disbelief
in the shepherd gets you a ticket to hell?

42:15.908 --> 42:17.868
Hey, Kang Ro-bin, you bastard!

42:18.369 --> 42:20.204
How dare you throw an adult up here!

42:20.871 --> 42:24.375
I did throw you, but you were the one
who got yourself stuck up there.

42:24.458 --> 42:25.417
Why, you…

42:26.502 --> 42:28.420
I ran so hard that I'm out of breath,

42:28.504 --> 42:30.506
so why isn't my heart racing?

42:30.589 --> 42:31.465
This is weird.

42:33.300 --> 42:35.177
Maybe you have to decide where to go.

42:35.261 --> 42:37.638
But there's nowhere
I want to go right now.

42:39.598 --> 42:43.435
I have to figure this out
so I can tell Master and show off.

42:47.314 --> 42:50.025
I'm just dying to show off!

42:52.152 --> 42:53.362
Chae-ni!

42:56.657 --> 42:57.825
No matter what,

42:59.076 --> 43:00.786
I will become Uri Geller.

43:01.996 --> 43:04.582
But why won't I get off?

43:11.505 --> 43:12.840
Pretty awesome!

43:13.507 --> 43:16.927
Hey, Master! I did it.

43:17.011 --> 43:19.930
I thought hard and focused like you said,
and I ended up--

43:25.561 --> 43:26.604
Run.

43:35.654 --> 43:37.823
-What the heck?
-Eun Chae-ni!

43:38.490 --> 43:39.992
Where's Master?

43:40.075 --> 43:41.327
It's just you. What is it?

43:43.120 --> 43:45.080
Master is in danger!

43:45.164 --> 43:47.875
You have to give
the who, what, when, where, why, and how.

43:47.958 --> 43:50.294
You can't just say he's in danger
and expect us to…

43:50.377 --> 43:51.920
Who am I even talking to?

43:52.421 --> 43:54.673
All the blood in my body
is rushing to my head.

43:54.757 --> 43:55.883
Someone get me down.

43:58.177 --> 43:59.762
What?

44:02.890 --> 44:04.141
What is that?

44:04.224 --> 44:05.476
Chae-ni! No!

44:06.018 --> 44:07.061
Get up.

44:10.731 --> 44:11.982
Chae-ni!

44:14.193 --> 44:16.195
Chae-ni!

44:17.321 --> 44:18.364
Master!

44:24.119 --> 44:25.371
Master.

44:27.247 --> 44:29.083
Now you've brought Kang Ro-bin too?

44:29.166 --> 44:30.000
Go back, now!

44:30.084 --> 44:31.669
We have to go together!

44:32.711 --> 44:33.545
Hey, Kang Ro-bin!

44:40.386 --> 44:41.470
Oh no!

44:41.553 --> 44:42.471
Focus.

44:48.227 --> 44:49.103
What are you doing?

44:49.186 --> 44:51.939
Hey, don't talk to me!
Why isn't it working?

44:52.523 --> 44:53.357
Let's go!

45:23.512 --> 45:25.180
What is this?

45:27.057 --> 45:28.058
He's a Wunderkinder.

45:39.987 --> 45:40.863
Hurry, go back.

45:40.946 --> 45:44.032
I'm dying to go back too.

45:46.034 --> 45:47.578
Chae-ni, what do we do?

45:47.661 --> 45:49.747
It looks like we're going to die here!

45:49.830 --> 45:51.832
Get off me and stop whining!

45:51.915 --> 45:52.958
Stop freeloading,

45:53.041 --> 45:56.712
and think of something
that'll actually help us yourself!

46:48.055 --> 46:49.181
No!

47:43.694 --> 47:46.113
Chae-ni! Did you see that?

47:46.655 --> 47:47.781
I just…

47:49.199 --> 47:50.492
Chae-ni!

47:51.660 --> 47:52.744
Where did Chae-ni…

47:53.370 --> 47:54.204
Chae-ni!

47:56.039 --> 47:57.082
Chae-ni!

48:21.148 --> 48:22.232
Ms. Eun Chae-ni!

48:23.734 --> 48:24.610
Ms. Chae-ni!

48:25.569 --> 48:26.820
Are you okay?

48:27.321 --> 48:28.322
Ms. Eun Chae-ni!

48:32.534 --> 48:33.827
This time,

48:35.162 --> 48:37.414
I actually did it.

48:40.834 --> 48:43.587
It's the northern lights.

49:01.480 --> 49:03.065
It's my first time

49:04.191 --> 49:06.443
being outside of Haeseong.

49:16.745 --> 49:18.246
It's beautiful.

49:30.509 --> 49:31.343
Hey.

49:32.010 --> 49:32.844
Ms. Eun Chae-ni.

49:34.012 --> 49:34.846
Ms. Eun Chae-ni!

49:35.347 --> 49:36.306
Ms. Eun Chae-ni!

49:54.324 --> 49:56.618
Chae-ni!

49:57.119 --> 49:58.578
Eun Chae-ni!

49:59.079 --> 50:02.249
How could you leave me here all alone?

50:06.545 --> 50:07.963
You scared me.

50:08.463 --> 50:10.632
You could've made some noise or something.

50:10.716 --> 50:11.883
And who are you?

50:13.176 --> 50:14.094
Another defective?

50:16.013 --> 50:16.930
Me?

50:17.514 --> 50:18.765
Who said I defected?

50:23.061 --> 50:27.566
If you're a Wunderkinder, that means
you also have a superpower, doesn't it?

50:32.988 --> 50:34.573
Why are you doing that?

51:13.445 --> 51:14.571
What are you doing?

51:16.865 --> 51:17.783
What are you?

51:18.366 --> 51:19.451
I'm Kang Ro-bin.

51:22.037 --> 51:24.372
Wait, why do you keep clapping?

51:28.460 --> 51:29.669
Should I be copying him?

51:32.005 --> 51:32.839
Boom pow?

51:35.509 --> 51:36.676
Boom boom pow!

51:39.554 --> 51:41.014
Boom boom pow!

51:41.098 --> 51:42.682
Boom boom pow!

51:42.766 --> 51:44.768
Boom boom pow!

51:44.851 --> 51:47.562
Boom boom pow! Is this it? Boom boom pow!

51:48.980 --> 51:50.148
Pow!

51:52.692 --> 51:54.319
This is it, right? Boom boom pow!

51:54.402 --> 51:56.238
Boom boom pow!

51:56.321 --> 51:57.405
Ha, ha, pow!

51:59.407 --> 52:04.037
I recently saw the historical drama
500 Years of the Joseon Dynasty.

52:04.663 --> 52:06.456
They had scapeghosts.

52:06.957 --> 52:08.708
Scapegoat, you mean.

52:08.792 --> 52:11.128
Anyway, they were basically goalies.

52:11.878 --> 52:15.715
They'd use their bodies
to block and absorb all the bad energy

52:15.799 --> 52:17.592
to protect the royal court.

52:36.736 --> 52:38.488
Peek-a-boo! Wait, not peek-a-boo.

52:38.572 --> 52:41.032
First of all,
I'm glad you're not too surprised.

52:41.116 --> 52:42.409
Deary me, this is…

52:42.492 --> 52:44.911
Right, I am Son Gyeong--

52:48.373 --> 52:49.833
Just a second.

52:50.375 --> 52:51.585
My head's spinning.

52:54.212 --> 52:55.088
I'm good now.

52:56.506 --> 52:59.342
You were… stuck up there?

53:00.552 --> 53:03.096
No. What do you mean "stuck"?

53:03.680 --> 53:06.391
I performed some magic tricks
for a talent show,

53:06.474 --> 53:07.601
